# last30days — API keys & configuration  (COMPLETE / full-scraping mode)
# ===========================================================================
# HOW TO USE
#   Local CLI:
#     cp .claude/last30days.env.example .claude/last30days.env
#     # fill in the keys you have, then lock it down:
#     chmod 600 .claude/last30days.env
#
#   Claude Code on the WEB:
#     This file is gitignored, so a fresh web clone will NOT contain your keys.
#     Set the SAME variable names as ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES / secrets in your
#     web environment's configuration. The engine reads plain env vars too.
#
# SECURITY: .claude/last30days.env is gitignored. NEVER commit real keys.
# Always-on sources needing NO key: Reddit (public), Hacker News, Polymarket.
# Everything below widens coverage to "complete" (social + Google + web).
# Full reference: .claude/skills/last30days/SKILL.md and upstream CONFIGURATION.md
# ===========================================================================

# --- Reasoning / planning provider (pick ONE) ------------------------------
# On Claude Code YOU are the planner, so this is optional; a key enables the
# headless / --auto-resolve path. Engine priority: Google > OpenAI > OpenRouter > xAI.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=          # also unlocks --deep-research (Perplexity, ~$0.90/query)
# XAI_API_KEY=                 # also usable as an X/Twitter backend (see below)

# --- Web / Google search backend (pick ONE) --------------------------------
# Powers --auto-resolve and the Step-2 web supplement (the "Google" layer).
# Serper is a Google Search API; Brave/Exa are alternatives (Brave has a free tier).
SERPER_API_KEY=                # Google search results — serper.dev
# BRAVE_API_KEY=               # Brave search (free tier) — brave.com/search/api
# EXA_API_KEY=                 # Exa neural search — exa.ai
# PARALLEL_API_KEY=

# --- Social scraping -------------------------------------------------------
# ScrapeCreators unlocks TikTok + Instagram + Threads + Pinterest (+ Reddit
# comments). 100 free credits, no card — scrapecreators.com (no affiliation).
# INCLUDE_SOURCES must list the platforms you want pulled.
SCRAPECREATORS_API_KEY=
INCLUDE_SOURCES=tiktok,instagram,threads,pinterest

# X / Twitter — pick ONE:
#   (a) Browser cookies, free: AUTH_TOKEN + CT0 from a logged-in x.com session
# AUTH_TOKEN=
# CT0=
#   (b) Cookie-jar from your local browser, free:
# FROM_BROWSER=firefox
#   (c) Paid API: set XAI_API_KEY above — it doubles as an X backend.

# Bluesky — free app password at bsky.app (Settings -> App passwords)
# BSKY_HANDLE=you.bsky.social
# BSKY_APP_PASSWORD=

# TruthSocial — free
# TRUTHSOCIAL_TOKEN=

# Apify — fallback scraper for Reddit/TikTok/Instagram when ScrapeCreators runs out
# APIFY_API_TOKEN=

# --- CLI-based sources (no key, install the tool) --------------------------
# GitHub : install `gh` and run `gh auth login`  -> GitHub source turns on.
# YouTube: install `yt-dlp`                       -> YouTube transcripts turn on.

# --- Storage / output ------------------------------------------------------
# Rendered briefs save here (default ~/Documents/Last30Days). Use an absolute
# path OUTSIDE this repo so research output is never accidentally committed.
# LAST30DAYS_MEMORY_DIR=/absolute/path/outside/repo
# LAST30DAYS_CONFIG_DIR=         # override global config dir; "" = no-config mode

# Silence the first-run setup wizard once you've configured keys above.
SETUP_COMPLETE=1
